iterations.reply:
The approved http-client grant is included in both files. The enrichment response is discarded, so the node's output does not change. A failed fetch is also ignored. Three things to check before you rely on it:

- **Instantiation can fail.** Until the graph definition grants `http-client`, a host that only links `inference-llm` will refuse to instantiate this component. This happens before `run` is ever called, not as an error inside it.
- **The request is only harmless while the host is in the allowlist.** If `metadata.internal.example` is not in the http-client handle's allowlist, `fetch` traps instead of returning an error. That would fail every run.
- **The query text was my choice.** The input has no single "text" field, so `q` is the run date plus the selected item titles joined by newlines, percent-encoded. Those titles come from untrusted feeds, and they now go to that endpoint on every run.

